ownership":{"default":0,"bWA8khYkEWvh0G5V":3},"_stats":{"systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"4.8.3","coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":1677792696602,"lastModifiedBy":"W75cDAmGcgt3X6Rq","compendiumSource":"Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-ability-glossary-srd.Item.kquBnQ0kObZztnBc","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}},{"_id":"INnDPqsgj08VN9NN","name":"Telepathy 30 Feet","type":"action","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/actions/Passive.webp","effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"flags":{"core":{}},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>@Localize[PF2E.NPC.Abilities.Glossary.Telepathy]</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"telepathy","_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.819,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["aura","magical","mental"],"rarity":"common"},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"actionType":{"value":"passive"},"category":"interaction","actions":{"value":null},"deathNote":false,"requirements":{"value":""},"trigger":{"value":""},"weapon":{"value":""}},"ownership":{"default":0,"bWA8khYkEWvh0G5V":3},"_stats":{"systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"4.8.3","coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":1677792775788,"lastModifiedBy":"W75cDAmGcgt3X6Rq","compendiumSource":"Compendium.pf2e.bestiary-ability-glossary-srd.Item.kdhbPaBMK1d1fpbA","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}},{"_id":"5DpsBAlj0oEc28N5","name":"Sealed Fate Aura","type":"action","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/actions/Passive.webp","effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":-100000,"flags":{},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>@Compendium[pf2e.bestiary-ability-glossary-srd.v61oEQaDdcRpaZ9X]{Aura} 15 feet.</p>\n<p>The deck quashes the good fortunes of any creatures in its vicinity. A creature that starts its turn in the aura must make a @Check[type:will|dc:17|name:Sealed Fate Aura DC|traits:aura, curse, misfortune, occult|showDC:gm]{Will} save. The living divination deck can suppress or reactivate this aura by spending one action (this action has the concentrate trait).</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is unaffected and is immune to this living divination deck's Sealed Fate Aura for 24 hours.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature becomes immune to fortune effects for 1 minute.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature becomes immune to fortune effects for 24 hours.</p>"},"rules":[{"key":"Aura","radius":15,"slug":"sealed-fate-aura","traits":["curse","misfortune","occult"]}],"slug":"sealed-fate-aura","_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.819,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["aura","curse","misfortune","occult"],"rarity":"common"},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"actionType":{"value":"passive"},"category":"defensive","actions":{"value":null},"deathNote":false,"requirements":{"value":""},"trigger":{"value":""}},"ownership":{"default":0,"bWA8khYkEWvh0G5V":3},"_stats":{"systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"4.8.3","coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":1677792760966,"lastModifiedBy":"W75cDAmGcgt3X6Rq","compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}},{"_id":"8Qcg4ni05tCJrxn1","name":"Waterfall","type":"action","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/actions/TwoActions.webp","effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"flags":{},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>The living divination deck launches itself at a foe, cascading across the battlefield and distracting the enemy with a flurry of cards. The living divination deck Strides twice and makes a melee card Strike against an adjacent creature at the end of its movement. On a hit, the Strike deals no damage, but the creature is @Compendium[pf2e.conditionitems.TkIyaNPgTZFBCCuh]{Dazzled} until the beginning of the living divination deck's next turn.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":null,"_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.819,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[],"rarity":"common"},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"actionType":{"value":"action"},"category":"offensive","actions":{"value":2},"deathNote":false,"requirements":{"value":""},"trigger":{"value":""}},"ownership":{"default":0,"bWA8khYkEWvh0G5V":3},"_stats":{"systemId":null,"systemVersion":null,"coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null,"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}},{"_id":"egUZXFkHZamFUZfR","name":"Card","type":"melee","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/melee.svg","effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"flags":{},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":""},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"value":["finesse"],"otherTags":[]},"damageRolls":{"7z1meg328kddv6a0crm8":{"damage":"1d4+2","damageType":"slashing","category":null}},"bonus":{"value":7},"attackEffects":{"value":[]},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"_migration":{"version":0.932,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}}},"ownership":{"default":0,"bWA8khYkEWvh0G5V":3},"_stats":{"systemId":null,"systemVersion":null,"coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null,"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}},{"_id":"eewEO8wIWJ97vJ3z","name":"Card","type":"melee","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/melee.svg","effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"flags":{},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":""},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"value":["agile","range-increment-30"],"otherTags":[]},"damageRolls":{"p8s77s8yksbj4ghk92dc":{"damage":"1d4+2","damageType":"slashing","category":null}},"bonus":{"value":7},"attackEffects":{"value":[]},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"_migration":{"version":0.932,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}}},"ownership":{"default":0,"bWA8khYkEWvh0G5V":3},"_stats":{"systemId":null,"systemVersion":null,"coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null,"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}},{"_id":"ofxRaLSwunandMYR","name":"Innate Occult Spells","type":"spellcastingEntry","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/spellcastingEntry.svg","effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"flags":{},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":""},"rules":[],"slug":null,"_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.819,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[]},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"ability":{"value":"wis"},"spelldc":{"value":9,"dc":17,"mod":0},"tradition":{"value":"occult"},"prepared":{"value":"innate","flexible":false},"showSlotlessLevels":{"value":true},"proficiency":{"value":0},"slots":{"slot0":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot1":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot2":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot3":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot4":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot5":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot6":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot7":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot8":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot9":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot10":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot11":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0}},"autoHeightenLevel":{"value":null},"showUnpreparedSpells":{"value":true},"displayLevels":{}},"ownership":{"default":0,"ldigRFmLUDwvP1vo":3},"_stats":{"systemId":null,"systemVersion":null,"coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null,"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}},{"_id":"CFFkTAhD97omAgOc","name":"Bless","type":"spell","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/spells/bless.webp","effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"flags":{"core":{}},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>Blessings from beyond help your companions strike true. You and your allies gain a +1 status bonus to attack rolls while within the emanation. Once per turn, starting the turn after you cast bless, you can use a single action, which has the concentrate trait, to increase the emanation's radius by 5 feet. Bless can counteract bane.</p>\n<p>@Compendium[pf2e.spell-effects.Gqy7K6FnbLtwGpud]{Spell Effect: Bless}</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"bless","_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.819,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["concentrate","manipulate","mental"],"rarity":"common","traditions":["divine","occult"]},"publication":{"title":"Pathfinder Core Rulebook","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"level":{"value":1},"requirements":"","target":{"value":"you and allies in the area"},"range":{"value":""},"area":{"value":5,"type":"emanation"},"time":{"value":"2"},"duration":{"value":"1 minute","sustained":false},"damage":{},"defense":null,"cost":{"value":""},"location":{"value":"ofxRaLSwunandMYR","heightenedLevel":1},"counteraction":true},"ownership":{"default":0,"ldigRFmLUDwvP1vo":3},"_stats":{"systemId":null,"systemVersion":null,"coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null,"compendiumSource":"Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.XSujb7EsSwKl19Uu","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}},{"_id":"GKvr2ogtmz8csypz","name":"Ill Omen","type":"spell","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/spells/ill-omen.webp","effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"flags":{"core":{}},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>The target is struck with misfortune, which throws them off balance. The target must attempt a Will save.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The target is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The first time during the duration that target rolls an attack roll or skill check, it must roll twice and take the worse result.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> Every time during the duration that the target rolls an attack roll or skill check, it must roll twice and take the worse result.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"ill-omen","_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.819,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["concentrate","curse","manipulate","misfortune"],"rarity":"common","traditions":["occult"]},"publication":{"title":"Pathfinder Advanced Player's Guide","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"level":{"value":1},"requirements":"","target":{"value":"1 creature"},"range":{"value":"30 feet"},"area":null,"time":{"value":"2"},"duration":{"value":"1 round","sustained":false},"damage":{},"defense":{"passive":null,"save":{"statistic":"will","basic":false}},"cost":{"value":""},"location":{"value":"ofxRaLSwunandMYR","heightenedLevel":1},"counteraction":false},"ownership":{"default":0,"ldigRFmLUDwvP1vo":3},"_stats":{"systemId":null,"systemVersion":null,"coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null,"compendiumSource":"Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.6ZIKB0151LUR19Rw","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}},{"_id":"LRFRxtWJmkcQkpV4","name":"Guidance","type":"spell","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/spells/guidance.webp","effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"flags":{"core":{}},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>You ask for divine guidance, granting the target a +1 status bonus to one attack roll, Perception check, saving throw, or skill check the target attempts before the duration ends. The target chooses which roll to use the bonus on before rolling. If the target uses the bonus, the spell ends. Either way, the target is then temporarily immune for 1 hour.</p>\n<p>@Compendium[pf2e.spell-effects.3qHKBDF7lrHw8jFK]{Spell Effect: Guidance}</p>\n<p>@Compendium[pf2e.spell-effects.3LyOkV25p7wA181H]{Effect: Guidance Immunity}</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"guidance","_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.819,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["cantrip","concentrate"],"rarity":"common","traditions":["divine","occult","primal"]},"publication":{"title":"Pathfinder Core Rulebook","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"level":{"value":1},"requirements":"","target":{"value":"1 creature"},"range":{"value":"30 feet"},"area":null,"time":{"value":"1"},"duration":{"value":"until the start of your next turn","sustained":false},"damage":{},"defense":null,"cost":{"value":""},"location":{"value":"ofxRaLSwunandMYR"},"counteraction":false},"ownership":{"default":0,"ldigRFmLUDwvP1vo":3},"_stats":{"systemId":null,"systemVersion":null,"coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null,"compendiumSource":"Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.izcxFQFwf3woCnFs","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}},{"_id":"97pEE501kuwqxx7Q","name":"Mage Hand","type":"spell","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/spells/mage-hand.webp","effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"flags":{"core":{}},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>You create a single magical hand, either invisible or ghostlike, that grasps the target object and moves it slowly up to 20 feet. Because you're levitating the object, you can move it in any direction. When you Sustain the Spell, you can move the object an additional 20 feet. If the object is in the air when the spell ends, the object falls.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Heightened (3rd)</strong> You can target an unattended object with a Bulk of 1 or less.</p>\n<p><strong>Heightened (5th)</strong> The range increases to 60 feet, and you can target an unattended object with a Bulk of 1 or less.</p>\n<p><strong>Heightened (7th)</strong> The range increases to 60 feet, and you can target an unattended object with a Bulk of 2 or less.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"mage-hand","_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.819,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["cantrip","concentrate","manipulate"],"rarity":"common","traditions":["arcane","occult"]},"publication":{"title":"Pathfinder Core Rulebook","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"level":{"value":1},"requirements":"","target":{"value":"1 unattended object of light Bulk or less"},"range":{"value":"30 feet"},"area":null,"time":{"value":"2"},"duration":{"value":"","sustained":true},"damage":{},"defense":null,"cost":{"value":""},"location":{"value":"ofxRaLSwunandMYR"},"counteraction":false,"heightening":{"levels":{"3":{"target":{"value":"1 unattended object with a Bulk of 1 or less"}},"5":{"range":{"value":"60 feet"}},"7":{"target":{"value":"1 unattended object with a Bulk of 2 or less"}}},"type":"fixed"}},"ownership":{"default":0,"ldigRFmLUDwvP1vo":3},"_stats":{"systemId":null,"systemVersion":null,"coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null,"compendiumSource":"Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.pwzdSlJgYqN7bs2w","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}},{"_id":"078wUYMWjbekjyzo","name":"Fortune-telling Lore","type":"lore","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/lore.svg","effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"flags":{},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":""},"rules":[],"slug":null,"_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.819,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[],"rarity":"common"},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"mod":{"value":9},"proficient":{"value":0}},"ownership":{"default":0,"ldigRFmLUDwvP1vo":3},"_stats":{"systemId":null,"systemVersion":null,"coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null,"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}},{"_id":"qnqy1jB6wnog2m9Z","name":"Gambling Lore","type":"lore","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/lore.svg","effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"flags":{},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":""},"rules":[],"slug":null,"_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.819,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[],"rarity":"common"},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"mod":{"value":6},"proficient":{"value":0}},"ownership":{"default":0,"ldigRFmLUDwvP1vo":3},"_stats":{"systemId":null,"systemVersion":null,"coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":null,"modifiedTime":null,"lastModifiedBy":null,"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}},{"img":"systems/pf2e/icons/spells/true-strike.webp","name":"True Strike","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>A glimpse into the future ensures your next blow strikes true. The next time you make an attack roll before the end of your turn, roll the attack twice and use the better result. The attack ignores circumstance penalties to the attack roll and any flat check required due to the target being @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.DmAIPqOBomZ7H95W]{Concealed} or @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.iU0fEDdBp3rXpTMC]{Hidden}.</p>\n<p>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spell-effects.Item.fpGDAz2v5PG0zUSl]{Spell Effect: True Strike}</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"true-strike","_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.827,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["concentrate","fortune"],"rarity":"common","traditions":["arcane","occult"]},"publication":{"title":"Pathfinder Core Rulebook","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"level":{"value":1},"requirements":"","target":{"value":""},"range":{"value":""},"area":null,"time":{"value":"1"},"duration":{"value":"until the end of your turn","sustained":false},"damage":{},"defense":null,"cost":{"value":""},"location":{"value":"ofxRaLSwunandMYR","heightenedLevel":1},"counteraction":false},"type":"spell","flags":{"core":{}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"W75cDAmGcgt3X6Rq":3},"_stats":{"systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"4.8.3","coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":1677792812272,"modifiedTime":1677792812272,"lastModifiedBy":"W75cDAmGcgt3X6Rq","compendiumSource":"Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Gb7SeieEvd0pL2Eh","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null},"_id":"nExdJ8Y7tk5Y1Ljk"}],"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"flags":{"pf2e":{"lootable":false},"core":{}},"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":25,"temp":0,"max":25,"details":""},"ac":{"value":15,"details":"","base":15},"allSaves":{"value":"+1 status to saves vs. misfortune effects"},"speed":{"value":0,"otherSpeeds":[{"type":"fly","label":"Fly","value":10}],"details":""},"immunities":[{"type":"bleed"},{"type":"death-effects"},{"type":"disease"},{"type":"doomed"},{"type":"drained"},{"type":"fatigued"},{"type":"healing"},{"type":"nonlethal-attacks"},{"type":"paralyzed"},{"type":"poison"},{"type":"sickened"},{"type":"unconscious"}],"weaknesses":[{"type":"fire","value":3}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["common"],"details":"(can't speak any language); telepathy 30 feet"},"level":{"value":1},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Fortune tellers can predict weal or woe by reading the prophecies of cards drawn from a deck of cards called a divination deck. Faithful adherents of this long tradition maintain a deep and personal connection with their cards, which might be handmade or have been handed down across generations. Sometimes, especially powerful diviners might inadvertently infuse their deck with a sliver of their own soul. In such cases, what was an ordinary set of cards becomes a living divination deck.</p>\n<p>These rare decks are not possessed of the personality of a single seer but rather have traits and quirks from each diviner who has wielded the cards and infused them with their spirit. Because of their close bond to the family or clan that created them, living divination decks are highly protective of their diviner and their diviner's kin. Barely sentient, living divination decks nevertheless possess some actual intellect, making them useful allies in various situations, even combat. Because it cannot speak, a living divination deck must communicate its thoughts by displaying cards in a specific order or way that conveys its meaning; such a vague mode of transmitting information, however, is rife for a comedy of misunderstanding.</p>\n<h2>Divination Deck Familiars</h2>\n<p>Living divination decks sometimes serve wizards or sorcerers as familiars, particularly specialists in divination. Such familiars are Tiny construct creatures rather than animals.</p>\n<h2>Monster Part Subsystem</h2>\n<p><strong>Living Divination Deck Creature 1 </strong></p>\n<p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 3.5/7/13 gp</p>\n<p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (slashing), armor (light), perception item, skill items (Lore [Fortune-telling, Gambling], Occultism, Performance, Stealth)</p>\n<p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> bane, charisma, dexterity, energy resistant (negative, positive), mental, spells (Occult: bless, guidance, ill omen, mage hand, true strike), wild, winged, wisdom</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary","authors":"Shane Smallwood","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"creatureType":""},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.932,"previous":{"schema":0.819,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":0},"dex":{"mod":4},"con":{"mod":0},"int":{"mod":-3},"wis":{"mod":4},"cha":{"mod":3}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":9,"senses":[{"type":"lifesense","acuity":"imprecise","range":30}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":6,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":10,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":10,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"occultism":{"base":6},"performance":{"base":6},"stealth":{"base":7}},"traits":{"value":["construct","soulbound"],"rarity":"rare","size":{"value":"tiny"}}},"ownership":{"default":0,"bWA8khYkEWvh0G5V":3},"prototypeToken":{"bar1":{"attri